  "proved": [
    "At chi=b/2 the frozen zero-edge Euler formula forces every region to have two trace sides and two old sides. The distinct-side hypothesis puts the old sides in distinct original tetrahedral faces.",
    "The old-side adjacency graph is a finite path for a boundary rectangle, and a finite cycle for a patch with no original boundary.",
    "The path gives a PL product rectangle cell by cell. A cycle gives an interval bundle; two trace boundary components exclude the reversing/Mobius monodromy, so an annular patch has a finite original-cell product parametrization."
